1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:14,800
A customer asks an AI assistant to move money, book a visit, settle a claim
or process a refund.

2
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:29,800
Rook helps connect that conversation to the behavior and evidence a team can
inspect.

3
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:44,800
Start by introducing the agent under test. Atlas Cover’s assistant reads
policies and claims, checks documents and requests settlements.

4
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:59,800
Its business tools determine what can be read or changed. The final answer
should agree with the recorded outcome.

5
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:14,800
Quality engineers start with requirements and a connection. Developers can
also provide source and inspect the implementation.

6
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:29,800
Both need a clear business rule and evidence that shows whether it held.
These demos provide a separate directory for each audience.

7
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:44,800
Jordan asks the insurance assistant to settle an eligible claim. Watch the
chat, then inspect the business receipt.

8
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:59,800
A tool call shows an attempt. A settlement receipt records the business
effect. Those observations answer different questions.

9
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:14,800
Now read a claim and refer to the same claim in the next turn. The agent
must preserve the customer’s context.

10
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:29,800
Rook’s multi-turn scenario keeps the turns in one conversation. A new
scenario starts with separate business state.

11
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:44,800
At Harbor Care, Alex asks for the eleven o’clock appointment. That slot has
no capacity.

12
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:59,800
The original recorded Rook check failed because an appointment was created.
This is a scheduling rule in a fictional service.

13
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:14,800
The updated healthcare check passed. The full-slot request was denied and
created no appointment.

14
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:29,800
Compare the response with the ledger. A friendly refusal and a correctly
enforced capacity rule should agree.

15
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:44,800
At Juniper Goods, Riley requests a refund while the payment provider is
unavailable.

16
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:59,800
The original recorded check failed: the assistant claimed success without a
refund receipt. Insurance showed the same kind of mismatch.

17
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:14,800
Move to Rook’s hosted web UI. Open the insurance agent and review its
functions and scenario collection.

18
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:29,800
There are eighteen authored categories in this edition. Authored starting
examples and newly generated scenarios must both be reviewed.

19
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:44,800
Open the dependency-failure scenario. The requirement is explicit: no
settlement receipt and no false claim of payment.

20
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:59,800
Review the goal, profile and criteria before interpreting the run. A result
without its test definition is easy to misunderstand.

21
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:14,800
Read the recorded result. The reply said the claim was settled while the
business evidence showed no settlement.

22
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:29,800
Rook retained the failure. A success-sounding answer did not replace the
missing payment receipt.

23
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:44,800
Follow the evidence for the exact conversation under test. Inspect the tool
name, arguments, returned result and trace.

24
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:59,800
Then read the business effects. Keep an attempted operation separate from a
completed action, and compare both with the final answer.

25
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:14,800
The updated insurance run passed the payment-failure check. Its reply
accurately reported that the settlement could not be completed.

26
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:29,800
The correlated evidence contained no settlement receipt. This is a verified
improvement for that selected case, not an all-category guarantee.

27
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:44,800
Red-teaming asks whether instructions or framing can push an agent beyond
its authorized behavior.

28
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:59,800
The collection includes role-play, prompt injection, disclosure, external
exports, hallucination, hijacking, harmful content, policy and technical
injection.

29
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:14,800
Treat protected content in an answer and an unauthorized export as separate
checks. A tool can block an export while a reply still discloses
information.

30
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:29,800
A recorded insurance run showed that distinction. Retain the failing
observation, then test the repair against the specific criterion.

31
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:44,800
The MCP profile is another way for Rook to invoke the same customer journey.
It supports a continuing conversation.

32
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:59,800
A separate read-only verifier checks the recorded business effects for that
conversation. Verification does not perform the business action again.

33
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:14,800
Pass means the required behavior is supported by evidence. Fail means a
required rule was observably violated.

34
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:29,800
Unable to Verify means the observation is missing or insufficient. It must
not be presented as a successful test.

35
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:44,800
Functional checks cover normal requests, invalid inputs, exact boundaries,
dependencies and context. Non-functional checks add reliability, speed, cost
and quality.

36
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:59,800
Measure latency using the recorded observations. Assess cost only when
provider usage is complete; missing usage cannot establish a passing budget.

37
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:14,800
The banking approval-limit check passed in both recorded versions because
the model refused the original request.

38
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:29,800
Show what happened instead of promising a failure. A refusal in one
conversation does not prove that every tool boundary is protected.

39
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:44,800
For regression demonstrations, the repository includes dated Rook samples
with their requests, responses, verdicts and business evidence.

40
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:59,800
The CI example checks those saved records. To evaluate a changed agent, run
new tests and review the evidence before updating the example.
